      "$note": [
        "cornerLabel, ringSides and compassPoint are WEB-ONLY presentation helpers",
        "for the boundary-tracing UI (RecordBoundary / FenceStudio). iOS takes side",
        "lengths and bearings server-derived through FMBGeometry.swift instead, so no",
        "Swift twin is owed for these three. Decided 13/09/2026.",
        "",
        "They are not silently divergent: core's ringSides().metres is haversine",
        "(ringPerimM, R=6371000) while Swift's boundarySideMetres projects",
        "equirectangularly, and at parcel scale the two agree to ~1.6 ppm — 0.1 mm on",
        "a 64 m side, far below the precision either head prints. Revisit only if a",
        "native screen starts computing side lengths for a user-traced ring."
      ]
    },
